NAVALM CUSTOM LICENSE AND UPSTREAM NOTICES
Version 1 — 23 September 2026

1. Attribution and scope

NAVALM is maintained by Chris Maness. Its astronomical engine is adapted
from the NAV48/NAV50 software developed by Dr. Thomas R. Metcalf and
distributed by Sparcom, subsequently ported to HP49/50 by Eddie C. Dost
and updated as NAV50 by Olivier M.P. Coignard. The C adaptation was
developed with AI-assisted translation of the available RPL source.

The underlying astronomy includes published methods described by Jean
Meeus and the VSOP87 planetary theory. Credit to Metcalf concerns the
upstream software implementation, not a claim that he originated all
the underlying mathematics. See PROVENANCE.md.

