This grant applies only to rights held by Chris Maness. It does not grant
permission on behalf of other copyright holders, expand the scope of
the upstream permissions, or override their restrictions. It places no
restriction on mathematical methods, facts, or material that is actually
in the public domain. No claim of copyright in purely AI-generated
material is made.

3. Upstream permissions and limits

The original statements below are preserved with their separate scopes.
Thomas Metcalf's 1994 permission accompanies the NAV48 Tricks and
Shortcuts supplement; it is not represented as a license for the entire
Sparcom ROM. Fred Metcalf's email accompanies Eddie Dost's patched
HP49/50 distribution. The NAV50 package credits Coignard but contains
no additional express license grant identified in its source or README.

The original Sparcom manual asserts corporate copyright. The supplied
materials do not establish a transfer of those rights to the Metcalf
family or expressly settle permission for every subsequent translation
and redistribution. This document records the available permissions;
it does not certify that all upstream rights have been cleared.

NAVALM is not offered as GPL-licensed or as a public-domain dedication.

