6. Eddie C. Dost's distribution README and Fred Metcalf's email (verbatim)

Source: nav-251.zip / README (also supplied as nav-251(1).zip).
Line endings normalized; original wording preserved.

This software has been developed by Dr. Thomas Metcalf and all credit
belongs to him.

After his tragic death and all activity around Sparcom ended, the
software was unmaintained. I contacted Thomas Metcalfs father and
was allowed to distribute the software patched for the HP49/50.

The HP49/50 library can only be installed to port 0, or IRAM, due to
size limitations in the flash banks.

README             - This file
nav-2.5.1-um.pdf   - The manual to the Sparcom Celestial Navigation Pac
nav-2.5.1.bin      - A dump of the Sparcom card for the HP48
nav-2.5.1.hp49.lib - The software ported to the HP49/50


Eddie C. Dost <ecd@brainaid.de>

========================================================================

Hello Eddie,

I am somewhat familiar with the software you're referring to.  I feel 
that I can say with complete confidence that Tom would have wanted his 
code to be maintained on sourceforge if he were no longer able to do so.

I do not have a copy of the original source, but will look on the 
machine left at his house in Boulder, Colorado when I'm there in late 
August.  Some of the less obvious calculations are described in some 
articles in the Journal of Navigation - several by Tom and a couple 
jointly with myself.

Please feel free to distribute the patched software as you see fit, 
simply acknowledging the origins of the code.

Fred Metcalf (Tom's father)
Professor of Mathematics, Emeritus

